    "text": "Yes, at two forty in the afternoon. I checked it this morning because I had written down two different times.\n\nIt is beside the green entrance. The patient form is available there, and I can ask them to check the spelling of my name.\n\nI have a small list. I want to describe a cough, a sore throat and a headache. I will not guess a temperature or say I have a fever if I have not measured it.\n\nI will describe where it is and when I first noticed it. I also wrote down a question about my stomach. The nurse can ask for any other information during the examination.\n\nYes. There is a pharmacy across the street. I have a question about a word on a medicine label, but I will ask the professional there rather than guess.\n\nDose. I will show the tablet package and ask what the label means. I will not decide what to take from the word alone.\n\nYes. My main question is what information they need. I will ask the nurse how to describe how I breathe and when I might recover. I will also ask for advice about my treatment.\n\nThanks. Please meet me by the yellow bench at three thirty, not at the green entrance. I will text you if the time changes.",
